
# DOM Events in React
DOM Events are actions that occur in the browser.

These actions can be:
- Button clicks
- Keyboard typing
- Mouse movement
- Form submission

React handles these events using:
Event Handlers

# What is DOM?

DOM stands for:

Document Object Model

DOM represents webpage structure as objects.

React interacts with DOM to update UI dynamically.

---

# Common DOM Events in React

| Event | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| onClick | Button click |
| onChange | Input value change |
| onSubmit | Form submit |
| onMouseOver | Mouse hover |
| onKeyDown | Keyboard press |

---

# Event Handlers in React

Event handlers are functions that execute when events occur.

---

# Syntax

onClick={functionName}